{
  "id": 125968159,
  "iid": 5065,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Don't close stdin on maxmind_db spawn error",
  "description": "This solves the following issue:\n\nIn cases where `mmdbresolve` fails to execute (e.g. when it's simply\nmissing from a tree) the spawn fails such that a zero initialized file\ndescriptor is closed (i.e. stdin). The close is silent, unless one\nexecutes something like `tshark -r - ...` where a bad file descriptor\nis reported then.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2021-11-12T22:35:24.269Z",
  "updated_at": "2021-11-18T21:03:03.849Z",
